{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Fk4dyQ9BePAHdzXyvAszSC","type":"tool_result","content":"1\t---\n2\tid: T-20260914-pilot-stdin\n3\ttitle: \"Validate resolved recipes from standard input\"\n4\tstatus: ready\n5\tformat_version: 3\n6\tprofile: standard\n7\teffort: S\n8\tbudget_iterations: 15\n9\tagent: claude\n10\tparent: (none)\n11\tdepends_on: []\n12\tsupersedes: (none)\n13\ttouches_paths: [src/recipe/recipes.py]\n14\tcreates_paths: []\n15\tsource_note: \"Registered reproduction: tests/fixtures/toolkit/pilot-reproduction.json recipe-stdin\"\n16\tcreated: \"2026-09-14T00:00:00Z\"\n17\ttags: []\n18\towner: (none)\n19\tpriority: P2\n20\tseverity: feature\n21\tdue_date: (none)\n22\tprecondition: (none)\n23\tblocked_reason: (none)\n24\tsecurity_class: (none)\n25\tsource_action_item: (none)\n26\ttracker_ref: (none)\n27\texecution_backend: claude\n28\tsigned_off: true\n29\tsigned_off_by: pilot-supervisor\n30\tsigned_off_at: 2026-09-14T20:30:55Z\n31\taccepted: false\n32\taccepted_by: (none)\n33\taccepted_at: (none)\n34\tsigned_off_sig: hmac-sha256-v3:15b16a06:922022e1e424ad644c6f8018b68a8e7abb557868ef329d039be67e7014bcfcf2\n35\t---\n36\t\n37\t# Validate resolved recipes from standard input\n38\t\n39\t> **Why:** A valid recipe piped to the documented CLI workflow is currently treated as a filename named dash.\n40\t\n41\t## Goal\n42\t\n43\tSupport recipe validate - for valid standard-input JSON while preserving file validation and rejecting malformed or invalid input.\n44\t\n45\t## Context\n46\t\n47\tThe user authorized a prospective real-repository-issue pilot. This isolated preflight uses one pinned provider invocation and does not count as a comparative run. The supervisor authorized only the declared Python file. Preserve all existing validation rules. Do not alter tests, specs, authorization, or signing material.\n48\t\n49\t## Behavior\n50\t\n51\t- **B-1** — GIVEN a valid recipe on stdin or in a file WHEN recipe validate is invoked THEN validation succeeds, while malformed and invalid documents fail with actionable diagnostics\n52\t\n53\t## Success Criteria\n54\t\n55\t```bash\n56\t# eval_1: Independent stdin, file, malformed-input, and validation-rule regressions\n57\teval_1() {\n58\t  /opt/homebrew/opt/python@3.14/bin/python3.14 /Users/luanmorenomaciel/GitHub/task-spec/tests/evals/toolkit/evaluate_issue.py small-fix --root .\n59\t}\n60\t\n61\t```\n62\t\n63\t## Validation Card\n64\t\n65\t```yaml\n66\tsuccess_criteria:\n67\t  - id: eval_1\n68\t    description: \"Independent stdin, file, malformed-input, and validation-rule regressions\"\n69\t    runnable: bash\n70\t    check_type: deterministic\n71\t    verifies: [B-1]\n72\t    terminal: true\n73\t    expected_duration_sec: 30\n74\tretry_policy:\n75\t  max_iterations: 15\n76\t  circuit_breaker_no_progress: 3\n77\t  on_terminal_failure: park_with_context\n78\tagent_contract:\n79\t  version: 2\n80\t  read: [intent, behavior, contract, guardrails]\n81\t  produce: [code, tests]\n82\t  required_tools: [git, bash]\n83\t  timeout_minutes: 30\n84\t  sandbox_type: host\n85\t  output_artifacts: []\n86\t  mcp_dependencies: []\n87\t  emit: [pass, fail, retry_with_reason, parked_with_context]\n88\t  backend_metadata: {}\n89\t```\n90\t\n91\t## Exit Check\n92\t\n93\t```bash\n94\teval_1\n95\t```\n96\t\n97\t## Rollback Plan\n98\t\n99\tRevert only the declared write surface and park the task with context.\n100\t\n101\t## Observability Hooks\n102\t\n103\t(none — no runtime observability required)\n104\t\n105\t## Anti-Patterns\n106\t\n107\t- Do not weaken or edit the eval contract after sign-off.\n108\t\n109\t## Do-Not-Touch\n110\t\n111\t- `spec`\n112\t- `tests`\n113\t- `tasks`\n114\t\n115\t## Open Questions\n116\t\n117\t(none — this task is fully specified)\n118\t"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"77455642-14bb-4183-bcc7-b8eb1521612f","uuid":"86cd69e8-358a-4892-8996-4aee3bf6aa82","timestamp":"2026-09-14T20:31:05.002Z","tool_use_result":{"type":"text",