{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5","id":"msg_011Cf3yMrcTiAmEyJJgNZm17","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"**Result: pass.** `T-20260914-pilot-stdin` is implemented and the declared evaluator passes.\n\n## Scope verification\nThe handoff (`TaskHandoff/v3`, tier 1, HMAC `hmac-sha256-v3:15b16a06:…`) matches the spec: single-member dependency closure, write scope `src/recipe/recipes.py` only, do-not-touch `spec`/`tests`/`tasks`. I changed only that one file; `git status` shows `M src/recipe/recipes.py` plus the pre-existing untracked `.taskspec/handoffs/`.\n\n## Root cause\n`recipes.py:103` passed the `validate` positional straight to `load_document`, which always does `Path(arg).read_text()`. So `-` was resolved as a literal filename — exactly the registered reproduction (`tests/fixtures/toolkit/pilot-reproduction.json`, issue `recipe-stdin`): `RECIPE=INVALID cannot read -: [Errno 2] No such file or directory: '-'`. I confirmed the baseline failure before editing.\n\n## Change\nAdded `load_input(source)`, which delegates to `load_document` for real paths and reads `sys.stdin` for `-`, following the existing repo idiom (`src/decompose/cli.py:227`, `src/evidence/operational.py:41`). The stdin branch mirrors `load_document`'s JSON-then-YAML-subset fallback *with the same strictness hooks*, so no validation rule is weakened on the new path; blank stdin gets its own actionable diagnostic, and the `validate` help now documents `-`. No validation logic, test, or eval contract was touched.\n\n## Evidence\n- Declared eval: `evaluate_issue.py small-fix` → `passed: true`, and `taskspec run --ci` → `eval_1 pass`, `_exit_check pass`. Repeated 3× identically (receipt requires determinism).\n- Parity spot-checks: file validation unchanged (`RECIPE=VALID`, and missing-file diagnostic intact); stdin JSON and YAML accepted; duplicate keys (`duplicate key 'runner'`), `NaN`, over-budget `max_rounds`, and empty stdin all still rejected with exit 1.\n- Regressions: `test-toolkit-cli.sh`, `test-toolkit-authoring.sh`, `test-toolkit-guides.sh`, `test-toolkit-install.sh` all PASS; both task gates verify Tier 1 HMAC unchanged.\n\nOne design note for your review, not a blocker: to keep stdin parsing byte-for-byte as strict as the file path, `load_input` imports `_json_object` and `_reject_json_constant` from `taskspec_data`. The cleaner fix is a public text-level loader in `src/lib/taskspec_data.py`, which is outside this task's authorized write surface — reproducing those two guards locally would have duplicated validation logic instead.\n\nNot committed, not accepted, no agents spawned, per the pilot constraints. No unresolved blockers."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":417,"cache_read_input_tokens":42913,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":417},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"77455642-14bb-4183-bcc7-b8eb1521612f","uuid":"b97f9a0d-55f6-4056-aa1e-c0165b76f471","timestamp":"2026-09-14T20:35:53.984Z","request_id":"req_011Cf3yMr8C54cgMLSFuFgPF"}
